From f6820689ff9f69bf2e61349ca78b306629e9bee7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taimoor Ul Islam <tislam@iastate.edu>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 12:13:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/52] kaiair: LDP core, deadline -> retransmission budget ->
 per-tx reliability (T-LDP.1)

pktr_ldp.h: pure-math LDP composition. N(D) in-deadline transmission opportunities
from (deadline, first-tx latency, HARQ retx cadence); required per-attempt
reliability p_req = 1-(1-beta_pkt)^(1/N); ldp_effective_tx_beta() is the single
composition point with the Cantelli loop, tight deadlines demand more power per
attempt, loose deadlines let HARQ absorb failures (the power-vs-latency trade).

Wired: env knobs KAIAIR_PKTR_DEADLINE_MS / PKT_BETA / TX0_MS / RETX_MS; the UL
actuation cushion and the metrics view/JSON now use the LDP-effective beta, and
the view prints a per-UE "PktR LDP" line (deadline, N, p_req, k vs static).

7 unit tests (budget floor/clamp/never-zero, p_req monotonicity + anchor 0.9 at
N=2, composition meets pkt target, cushion shrinks with looser deadline,
disabled passthrough). All pass; gnb builds clean.
